    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Bryson Stott** (68.86) anchor our lineup as the highest-projected efficiency plays. **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Fedde (5.20 xERA) in a hitter-friendly park, coupled with the wind blowing out, which offsets the minor drag from a dynamic platoon disadvantage. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** receives a significant boost from a favorable 13% platoon edge and the opportunity to exploit a slower opposing battery, keeping him well above the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold despite the minor speed bump of facing an elite defensive catcher. **Dylan Beavers** also profiles as an elite start at 68.38; his aggressive placement in the #3 spot and a massive 19% SP skill advantage against Fedde make him a high-upside play for both run production and speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Daulton Varsho** on the bench. With a score of 49.53, he remained in the \"Marginal\" category but fell just short of our rotation requirements due to a significant 17% penalty against his matchup. The optimizer prioritized the consistency of **Masyn Winn** and the higher-order upside of **Geraldo Perdomo**, even though both faced tough defensive setups. We are closely monitoring the weather at the Pfaadt-hosted contests, as any shifts in the wind could further depress the efficiency of **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert**. While we are currently comfortable with **Cal Raleigh** and **Jonathan Aranda** in their respective roles, both carry lower floors tonight, and we are prepared to pivot if the pre-game lineups indicate any late-hour rest or tactical shifts. **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remain sidelined, underscoring the importance of our depth players staying above the 40-point floor.",
